<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
  <%- include('common/head.ejs', { pageTitle: 'Privacy Policy' }) %>
  <body>
    <%- include('common/header.ejs') %>
    <main class="main">
      <div class="main-item vflex align-items-stretch">
        <div class="py-4">
          <h2 class="heading-noline display-6">Overview</h2>
          <hr class="divider my-2" />
          <p>
            Cedar Groves Executive Par 3 &amp; Driving Range ("we", "us", or
            "our") respects your privacy and is committed to
            protecting the personal information you share with us. This Privacy
            Policy explains how we collect, use, disclose, retain, and protect
            personal information when you visit cedargrovesgolf.ca (the
            "website") or contact us through it, and describes the choices and
            rights available to you.
          </p>
          <p>
            In this policy, "personal information" means information about an
            identifiable individual, such as your name, email address, or the
            content of a message you send us. We handle personal information in
            accordance with Canada's Personal Information Protection and
            Electronic Documents Act (PIPEDA) and other applicable privacy laws.
          </p>
          <p>
            By using the website, you acknowledge that you have read and
            understood this policy. If you do not agree with it, please do not
            submit personal information through the website.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="py-4">
          <h2 class="heading-noline display-6">Information we collect</h2>
          <hr class="divider my-2" />
          <p>
            <strong>Information you provide.</strong> We collect personal
            information that you choose to give us, for example when you send us
            a message or ask a question. This may include your name, email
            address, the subject of your inquiry, and any other details you
            include in your message. You decide what to share, and we ask that
            you not send sensitive information that is not needed to respond to
            you.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>Information collected automatically.</strong> When you visit
            the website, certain technical information is collected
            automatically, as is standard for most websites. This may include
            your IP address, browser type and version, device type, operating
            system, the date and time of your visit, and the pages you request.
            This information is used to deliver the website to your device, keep
            it secure, protect it from spam and misuse, and diagnose technical
            problems. We do not use it to build profiles of individual visitors.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>Children's privacy.</strong> The website is intended for a
            general audience and is not directed to children under the age of
            13. We do not knowingly collect personal information from children.
            If you believe a child has provided us with personal information,
            please contact us and we will delete it.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="py-4">
          <h2 class="heading-noline display-6">How we use your information</h2>
          <hr class="divider my-2" />
          <p>
            We collect and use personal information only for purposes that a
            reasonable person would consider appropriate in the circumstances,
            and we limit what we collect to what is needed for those purposes.
            Specifically, we use personal information:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>To respond to your questions, requests, and other communications.</li>
            <li>To provide information about our course, rates, memberships, and services that you have asked about.</li>
            <li>To protect the website and our visitors from spam, fraud, abuse, and security threats.</li>
            <li>To operate, maintain, troubleshoot, and improve the website.</li>
            <li>To comply with our legal obligations and respond to lawful requests from authorities.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            <strong>Consent.</strong> By submitting information through the
            website, you consent to its collection and use for the purposes
            described in this policy. If we wish to use your information for a
            new purpose, we will ask for your consent first, unless the law
            permits or requires otherwise. You may withdraw your consent at any
            time, subject to legal or contractual restrictions, by contacting us
            using the details below.
          </p>
          <p>
            We do not sell, rent, or trade your personal information, and we do
            not use it for advertising or marketing unless you have asked to
            hear from us.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="py-4">
          <h2 class="heading-noline display-6">Service providers</h2>
          <hr class="divider my-2" />
          <p>
            Like most small businesses, we rely on trusted third-party service
            providers to operate the website, including providers of website
            hosting, email, and spam protection. These providers process
            personal information on our behalf, only as needed to provide their
            services to us, and are expected to protect it in a manner consistent
            with this policy. We do not otherwise share your personal information
            with third parties, except where required by law, to protect our
            rights or the safety of others, or with your consent.
          </p>
          <p>
            Some of our service providers may store or process information
            outside Canada, including in the United States. While in another
            country, your information is subject to the laws of that country and
            may be accessible to its courts, law enforcement, and national
            security authorities.
          </p>
          <p>
            This website uses Google reCAPTCHA to protect against spam and abuse.
            reCAPTCHA collects hardware and software information, such as device
            and application data, and sends it to Google for analysis. Its use is
            subject to Google's
            <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="color-gold hover transition">Privacy Policy</a>
            and
            <a href="https://policies.google.com/terms" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="color-gold hover transition">Terms of Service</a>.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>Third-party websites.</strong> The website may contain links
            to websites and services operated by others, such as social media
            platforms and review sites. We are not responsible for the content or
            privacy practices of those sites, and we encourage you to review
            their privacy policies before providing them with any personal
            information.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="py-4">
          <h2 class="heading-noline display-6">Cookies</h2>
          <hr class="divider my-2" />
          <p>
            Cookies are small text files that a website stores in your browser.
            We use cookies only where they are strictly necessary for the website
            to work and to keep it secure, for example to protect forms against
            spam and to support sign-in for staff who manage the website. Some of
            these cookies may be set by our service providers.
          </p>
          <p>
            We do not use cookies for advertising, analytics, or tracking you
            across other websites. Most browsers let you view, block, or delete
            cookies through their settings. If you choose to block cookies, some
            features of the website, such as the contact form, may not work as
            intended.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="py-4">
          <h2 class="heading-noline display-6">Retention</h2>
          <hr class="divider my-2" />
          <p>
            We keep personal information only for as long as it is needed to
            fulfil the purposes described in this policy, including responding
            to you and maintaining reasonable business records, or for as long as
            required or permitted by law. When personal information is no longer
            needed, we delete it or make it anonymous.
          </p>
          <p>
            Technical information collected automatically is kept for a limited
            period for security and troubleshooting purposes and is then deleted
            automatically. If personal information has been used to make a
            decision about you, we keep it long enough to allow you to access it.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="py-4">
          <h2 class="heading-noline display-6">Security</h2>
          <hr class="divider my-2" />
          <p>
            We use reasonable physical, organizational, and technical safeguards
            appropriate to the sensitivity of the information to protect personal
            information against loss, theft, and unauthorized access, use,
            disclosure, copying, or modification. These safeguards include
            encrypted connections to the website, restricting access to those
            who need it, and relying on reputable service providers that maintain
            their own security programs.
          </p>
          <p>
            No method of transmitting or storing information over the internet
            is completely secure, so we cannot guarantee absolute security. If a
            breach of security involving your personal information creates a real
            risk of significant harm, we will notify you and the Office of the
            Privacy Commissioner of Canada as required by law.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="py-4">
          <h2 class="heading-noline display-6">Your rights</h2>
          <hr class="divider my-2" />
          <p>
            Subject to certain exceptions set out in law, you have the right to
            ask whether we hold personal information about you, to access that
            information, and to be told how it has been used and to whom it has
            been disclosed. If any of your personal information is inaccurate or
            incomplete, you may ask us to correct it. You may also withdraw your
            consent and ask us to delete your personal information, unless we are
            required to keep it by law.
          </p>
          <p>
            To make a request, contact us using the details below. We may need
            to verify your identity before responding, and we will respond within
            the time required by law, generally within 30 days. There is no
            charge for most requests.
          </p>
          <p>
            If you have a concern about how we have handled your personal
            information, please contact us first so we can try to resolve it. If
            you are not satisfied with our response, you have the right to file a
            complaint with the
            <a href="https://www.priv.gc.ca" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="color-gold hover transition">Office of the Privacy Commissioner of Canada</a>.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="py-4">
          <h2 class="heading-noline display-6">Changes to this policy</h2>
          <hr class="divider my-2" />
          <p>
            We may update this policy from time to time to reflect changes in our
            practices, our service providers, or applicable law. When we do, we
            will post the updated policy on this page and revise the "Last
            updated" date below. Changes take effect when they are posted. We
            encourage you to review this policy periodically, and your continued
            use of the website after changes are posted means you accept the
            updated policy.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="py-4">
          <h2 class="heading-noline display-6">Contact us</h2>
          <hr class="divider my-2" />
          <p>
            We have designated an individual who is accountable for our
            compliance with this policy and with applicable privacy laws. If you
            have questions,
            requests, or concerns about this policy or about how we handle your
            personal information, please contact us:
          </p>
          <p>
            Cedar Groves Executive Par 3 &amp; Driving Range
            <br />
            2000 Golden Grove Road, Saint John, NB, E2N 2A1
            <br />
            <a href="mailto:contact@cedargrovesgolf.ca" class="color-gold hover transition">contact@cedargrovesgolf.ca</a>
            <br />
            <a href="tel:5068477273" class="color-gold hover transition">(506) 847-7273</a>
          </p>
          <p class="mb-0"><em>Last updated: November 2026</em></p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </main>
    <%- include('common/footer.html') %>
  </body>
</html>
